{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles and its motion capabilities, separating sensing and actuation. The specification automata E1 encodes the conservative exploration and obstacle avoidance policy: random_walk is preferred in clear, move_forward is used only for short progress, and right turns are preferred for recovery. Obstacle events force deterministic turn-based recovery, and random_walk/move_forward are never enabled in obstacle states. All uncontrollable events are total in every state. The design ensures no infinite controllable loops, no oscillation, and no unsafe forward actions in obstacle states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion to allow modular specification.",
    "Specification automaton encodes conservative exploration, deterministic obstacle recovery, and right-turn preference."
